# Files that may reach main without the founder's approval (founder, 9 Oct 2026: tooling
# merges after both reviews; option (ii) for release machinery). founder-gate reads this
# copy on main, never the pull request's, and the release refuses any other file that
# changed since the last verified release unless the founder approved its pull request.
#
# One pattern per line, from the repo root. The last line that matches a file decides.
#   A <pattern>   tooling that never runs in a release
#   B <pattern>   release machinery: both reviews say whether it weakens a check on production
#                 access, secrets, the deploy hold or branch rules (if so, the founder
#                 approves), and a REAL rehearsal on the rehearsal copy passes first
#   ! <pattern>   never on the list: the founder approves
# * matches within one folder; ** matches across folders.

# A: never runs in a release
A ops/release/server/README.md
A tests/**
A tooling/**
A docs/**
A sandbox/**

# B: release machinery, which runs with the deploy key or on production (after A, so these
# win inside sandbox)
B ops/release/ci/**
# The release runner: deploys refuse until the founder installs the newest one, and it runs on
# every deploy and undo, so it is release machinery, not tooling.
B ops/release/server/**
A ops/release/server/README.md
B sandbox/lib/**
B scripts/**

# Never on the list
# install.sh and the forced commands decide what each key may do on the server.
! ops/release/server/install.sh
! ops/release/server/release-command
! ops/release/server/maintenance-command
! ops/release/server/read-command
! ops/release/server/app-errors.py
# The protected-schema guard: a change here changes a production data check.
! ops/release/server/guarded-schema.py
! ops/release/server/public-schema.sql
! docs/decisions/**
! docs/decisions-*
! docs/accepted-capabilities.md
